Z||000000||8Ball||11-11-2001||09:10 PM||||Ok I will probably never find this but it is worth a try. <P>I am looking for new carpet for the Fiero. Same looped style as the factory carpet, but I want it in deep purple. I thought about dyeing the carpet I have now, but I strongly doubt it would hold the color under wear for long.<P>If anyone knows where I could find some, or has a success story of the longevity of dyed carpet. Please let me know.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Nashco||11-11-2001||09:23 PM||||I've heard good things about this company:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.accmats.com/main.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.accmats.com/main.html</A> <P>Enough good things that I plan on ordering my carpet from them when the time comes.  A few forum members use their carpet, and say it's not as heavy, but fits well.  I'm not sure about what colors are offered, but you can check it out, I'm sure there's something they could do.  I'm pretty sure you can order any color.  Good luck, and let us know what you decide.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||avengador1||11-11-2001||09:35 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.1aautomotive.com" TARGET=_blank>www.1aautomotive.com</A>  has carpets for the Fiero in different loops and colors, if you want to check them out.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
