Z||000004||Nashco||11-11-2001||10:08 PM||||I've been told that 1aautomotive gets their carpets from AAC, does anybody know if this is true?  I checked out prices on 1aautomotive.com, and theirs are 133 bucks, compared to 170 from AAC.  If the quality is the same, it may be better to go with 1aautomotive.  I'm about three miles from AAC, so I'll go with them anyway, otherwise I'm not sure <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||BAM-BAM||11-11-2001||10:25 PM||||I put my ACC Carpet in today. I had been holding off because I was afraid of what hassles I would run in to. Well, what an idiot I am, it all went in extremely easy. It fit perfect. You do have to cut the holes for the trim panels, seatbelt anchors and don't forget the hold down tabs in the front right on the driver side and front left on the passenger side. AutoZone or the like carry them. I will take some pics in the morning for all to see. It looks awesome and my custom mats look even better. <BR>  When I pulled the old carpet out I left the under matting to help deaden any road noise and add a more comfortable, cushier feel to the carpet. It was a breeze!!!!<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Spiff||11-11-2001||11:54 PM||||A1Automotive does get their carpet from ACC.<BR>I got a set off of E-Bay earlier this year and was extremely happy with the results. I paid $109 for the on E-Bay, but then I also got the floor mats, embroidery and extra carpet. IIRC I think the total with everything was like $220-230. Great carpet and easy to install.<BR>||||reg||1
